From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove@yandex.ru>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:56:03 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 124/202] Meridian: a press on the window's drag area or edge
 stays with the window on Windows

The window still couldn't be dragged: a press on the top bar went down into
the UI page, which took it, so Windows never got to start the move. On
Windows the window now keeps such presses to itself, as it already did on
ChromeOS for the caption: where it answers "caption" or a resize edge, the
event doesn't descend into the page.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../browser/ui/webui_browser/webui_browser_window.cc | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/webui_browser/webui_browser_window.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/webui_browser/webui_browser_window.cc
index ae0686c441..a60a1aaada 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/webui_browser/webui_browser_window.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/webui_browser/webui_browser_window.cc
@@ -1490,6 +1490,18 @@ bool WebUIBrowserWindow::WidgetDelegate::ShouldDescendIntoChildForEventHandling(
     return false;
   }
   return true;
+#elif BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN)
+  // Meridian: the same on Windows, where the window has no title bar of its
+  // own (webui_browser_frame_view_win.h). A press on the page's drag area or
+  // on a resize edge must not go down into the page, which would take it:
+  // left to the window, Windows starts the move or the resize.
+  if (GetWidget()) {
+    const int component = GetWidget()->GetNonClientComponent(location);
+    if (component != HTCLIENT && component != HTNOWHERE) {
+      return false;
+    }
+  }
+  return true;
 #else
   // Other platforms such as Windows do hit testing (WM_NCHITTEST) before
   // sending pointer events. That happens before aura::Window has a chance to
